<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>8.3.5: Practice</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m02131</md:content-id>
    <md:title>8.3.5: Practice</md:title>
    <md:uuid>e12d3f31-0e54-4cca-95e6-e2f50a9a6e5c</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><para>Complete the following questions to practice the skills you have learned in this lesson.</para>
<section class="check-understanding"><exercise id="c71e7ef2-74df-4658-9a44-e9c3c913a8a2" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>For questions 1 - 2, determine the number of solutions. Then solve the equation.</para><para>\(3x^2=48\)</para>
      <para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>0 solutions</para><para>1 solution; \(x=4\)</para><para>2 solutions; \(x=4\) and \(x=-4\)</para><para>2 solutions; \(x=12\) and \(x=-12\)</para></problem><solution><para>Correct!</para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 8.3.1. </para><para>The correct answer is two solutions; \(x=4\) and \(x=-4\). </para></solution></exercise><exercise id="8133ca1e-ea57-40c5-ac3c-74388fe6fc6c" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>\((x+2)(x+2)=0\)</para>
      <para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>0 solutions</para><para>1 solution; \(x=-2\)</para><para>1 solution; \(x=2\)</para><para>2 solutions; \(x=2\) and \(x=-2\)</para></problem><solution><para>Correct!</para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 8.3.1.</para><para>The correct answer is one solution; \(x=-2\). </para></solution></exercise><exercise id="41b5f66f-90c1-413f-9e3a-6007000edeea" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>For questions 3 – 10, solve the quadratic equation.</para><para>\(4m^2=36\)</para>
      <para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>\(m=3\) and \(m=-3\)</para><para>\( m=3\)</para><para>\( m=9\) and \(m=-9\)</para><para>\(m=2\) and \(m=-2\)</para></problem><solution><para>Correct!</para><para>Try again. Revisit activities 8.3.2 and 8.3.4. </para><para>The correct answer is \(m=3\) and \(m=-3\). </para></solution></exercise><exercise id="9d2defef-d0de-4715-b977-fb1f2cce5468" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>\(d^2-25=0\)</para>
      <para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>\(d=5\) and \(d=-5\)</para><para>\(d=5\)</para><para>\(d=-5\)</para><para>\(d=25\)</para></problem><solution><para>Correct!</para><para>Try again. Revisit activities 8.3.2 and 8.3.4.</para><para>The correct answer is \(d = 5\) and \(d = -5\). </para></solution></exercise><exercise id="3b3a88e1-ee15-4f86-bd00-3f793f0c65d1" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>\(\frac{2}{3}z^2=54\)</para>
      <para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>\(z=6\) and \(z=-6\)</para><para>\(z=7\) and \(z=-9\)</para><para>\(z=9\) and \(z=-9\)</para><para>\(z=7\) and \(z=-7\)</para></problem><solution><para>Correct!</para><para>Try again. Revisit activities 8.3.2 and 8.3.4. </para><para>The correct answer is \(z=9\) and \(z=-9\). </para></solution></exercise><exercise id="77e0882d-16e7-4b13-b56f-6677ede5e696" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>\(4p^2+10=266\)</para>
      <para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>\(p=18\) and \(p=-18\)</para><para>\(p=12\) and \(p=-12\)</para><para>\(p =16\) and \(p=-16\)</para><para>\(p=8\) and \(p=-8\)</para></problem><solution><para>Correct!</para><para>Try again. Revisit activities 8.3.2 and 8.3.4.</para><para>The correct answer is \(p=8\) and \(p=-8\). </para></solution></exercise><exercise id="6feca9eb-d756-4000-8edd-4f088dd1c31a" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>\((a−7)^2+5=105\)</para>
      <para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>\(a=17\) and \(a=-3\)</para><para>\(a=-17\) and \(a=3\)</para><para>\(a=-10\) and \(a=10\)</para><para>\(a=3\) and \(a=-3\)</para></problem><solution><para>Correct!</para><para>Try again. Revisit activities 8.3.3 and 8.3.4. </para><para>The correct answer is \(a=17\) and \(a=-3\). </para></solution></exercise><exercise id="45a90896-1755-48af-b75f-11307359e21c" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>\((b−1)^2−9=55\)</para>
      <para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>\(b=9\) and \(b=-9\)</para><para>\(b=8\) and \(b=-8\)</para><para>\(b=9\) and \(b=-7\)</para><para>\(b=-9\) and \(b=7\)</para></problem><solution><para>Correct!</para><para>Try again. Revisit activities 8.3.3 and 8.3.4.</para><para>The correct answer is \(b =9\) and \(b=-7\). </para></solution></exercise><exercise id="c22605f5-d305-48f1-85f7-248c039ca492" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>\(\frac17(x+3)^2−5=2\)</para>
      <para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>\(x=-4\) and \(x=10\)</para><para>\(x=4\) and \(x=-10\)</para><para>\(x=-4\) and \(x=4\)</para><para>\(x=-2\) and \(x=12\)</para></problem><solution><para>Correct!</para><para>Try again. Revisit activities 8.3.3 and 8.3.4. </para><para>The correct answer is \(x=4\) and \(x=-10\). </para></solution></exercise><exercise id="1e9bfb23-6bef-4dc8-89f1-e2f77672912b" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>\(5(x−8)^2−7=118\)</para>
      <para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>\(x=13\) and \(x=3\)</para><para>\(x=-3\) and \(x=-13\)</para><para>\(x=5\) and \(x=-5\)</para><para>\(x=5\) and \(x=-11\)</para></problem><solution><para>Correct!</para><para>Try again. Revisit activities 8.3.3 and 8.3.4.</para><para>The correct answer is \(x=13\) and \(x=3\). </para></solution></exercise></section></section>
